[00:00.62] (Rex Griffin)
[00:14.26] Why do you treat me as if I was only a friend
[00:24.86] What have I done that has made you so different and cold
[00:37.14] Sometimes I wonder if you'll be contented again
[00:50.20] Will you be happy when you are withered and old.
[01:17.86] --- Instrumental ---
[01:17.86] I cannot offer you diamonds or mansions so fine
[01:28.16] I cannot buy you the clothes that your young body crave
[01:41.86] But if you'll say that you long to forever be mine
[01:54.00] Think of the heartaches the sorrow the teardrops you'll save.
[02:14.32] --- Instrumental ---
[02:21.36] When you grow weary and tired of another's caress
[02:32.00] When you are lonely remember this letter my own
[02:45.72] But don't try to answer for there's one thing I'll have to confess
[02:57.34] If you don't love me, I wish you would leave me alone...
